# 30. Simple Educational OSINT Tool

The following example combines basic concepts.

```python
import requests
import socket
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

target = input("Enter authorized domain: ").strip()

if not target.startswith(("http://", "https://")):
    url = "https://" + target
else:
    url = target

hostname = url.split("://", 1)[1].split("/", 1)[0]

print("\n[+] Target:", hostname)

# DNS lookup
try:
    ip = socket.gethostbyname(hostname)
    print("[+] IP Address:", ip)
except socket.gaierror:
    print("[-] DNS lookup failed")
    ip = None

# HTTP request
try:
    response = requests.get(
        url,
        timeout=10,
        headers={
            "User-Agent": "Educational-OSINT-Tool/1.0"
        }
    )

    print("[+] HTTP Status:", response.status_code)

    soup = BeautifulSoup(
        response.text,
        "html.parser"
    )

    if soup.title:
        print("[+] Page Title:",
              soup.title.get_text(strip=True))
    else:
        print("[-] No page title found")

    print("[+] Public Links:")

    for link in soup.find_all("a", href=True):
        print("   ", link["href"])

except requests.exceptions.RequestException as e:
    print("[-] HTTP request failed:", e)
```

### What this tool demonstrates

```text
User Input
    ↓
Target Parsing
    ↓
DNS Lookup
    ↓
HTTP Request
    ↓
HTML Parsing
    ↓
Title Extraction
    ↓
Link Extraction
```

